Big O notation
---------------
Big O notation is a way to measure the time and space complexity of an algorithm

O(1) - Constant (Fastest, e.g., accessing an array by index)
O(log N) - Logarithmic (e.g., Binary Search)
if an array has 8 element which  2^3 the O(LogN)=3  default log base is 2
O(N) - Linear (e.g., A simple for loop)
O(N log N) - Linearithmic (e.g., Most efficient sorting)
O(N²) - Quadratic (Slow, e.g., Nested for loops)